Statement: "Most of the time is spent in the event handlers (processing duration), so a faster network or CDN will not fix this INP; the handler work has to shrink or yield."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. INP measures from the tap to the next frame on screen: input delay (waiting for the main thread), processing duration (the event handlers) and presentation delay (rendering the frame). Here 540 of 610 ms are the handlers themselves, work done on the main thread after the tap. No request is part of that number; the fix is less work in the handler, or yielding so the frame can paint first (next lesson).', 3, 5
